Entries start with "* ".


1. Assets inside this package (tess_shell/)

* shipped/Icons/mdi.json: the Material Design Icons set (icon prefix "mdi") by
  Pictogrammers, https://github.com/Templarian/MaterialDesign, in Iconify's JSON
  form. Licence: Apache-2.0 (the set's own "license" field says Apache-2.0).
  Pictogrammers state that some of the icons are redistributed under their
  respective licences and the others under Apache-2.0; the set as a whole is
  distributed under the licence provided with it, and no per-icon list ships.
  The Apache License 2.0 text is at https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.

* shipped/Icons/MDI-LICENSE.txt: the Pictogrammers Free License text that comes
  with the icon set (icons and fonts Apache-2.0, code MIT). It must stay next to
  mdi.json.

* shipped/Icons/NOTICE.txt: the attribution note for mdi.json, by this project.

* shipped/Handles/tess_shell_bar.svg
* shipped/Handles/tess_shell_chevron.svg
* shipped/Handles/tess_shell_dots.svg: the three handle icons of a peek,
  artwork made by the maintainer for Tesserae Shell and flattened from his
  Inkscape files. Licence: MIT, the licence of this package (LICENSE).

* shipped/Handles/NOTICE.txt: the note that says so, by this project.

* shipped/Images/error.png: the 64 x 64 image shown in place of an image that
  cannot be decoded (a grey rounded square with a red cross). Made for
  Tesserae Shell; no third-party source is recorded for it. Licence: MIT, the
  licence of this package (LICENSE).

The package ships no font. Text is drawn with the fonts bundled in
tesserae-engine (section 2).


2. Assets and components bundled by tesserae-engine (tess_re)

tesserae-engine 0.6.x ships one compiled extension, tess_re/_core*.so, and
five shared libraries beside it. The shell's text, layout and drawing run
through it. The licence of tesserae-engine itself is MIT. Checked against the
0.6.9 wheel; the range in section 3 is the range this was checked for.

* Roboto-Regular and Roboto-Medium (the engine's default typeface; the shell's
  `type.system.font_family` token holds "Roboto"): Google's Roboto 2.137,
  embedded in _core*.so. Licence: Apache-2.0 (the fonts' own name table says
  "Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0",
  http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Copyright 2011 Google Inc.
  Source: https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Roboto

* Noto Sans Arabic Regular 2.013: embedded in _core*.so. Licence: SIL Open
  Font License 1.1 (https://openfontlicense.org). Copyright 2022 The Noto
  Project Authors, https://github.com/notofonts/arabic

* Hack Nerd Font Mono Regular (Nerd Fonts 3.5.1 patch of Hack): embedded in
  _core*.so. Licence: MIT for the Hack project (Copyright 2018 Source Foundry
  Authors, https://github.com/source-foundry/Hack), public domain for the DejaVu
  work it derives from, and the Bitstream Vera License for Bitstream Vera Sans
  Mono (Copyright 2003 Bitstream, Inc.). The font's name table carries these
  terms. Source: https://www.nerdfonts.com/font-downloads

* Rust crates linked statically into _core*.so: 495 crates (among them vello,
  parley, peniko, kurbo, accesskit, pyo3), each listed with its name, version
  and SPDX licence expression in the wheel's
  tesserae_engine-*.dist-info/sboms/engine-py.cyclonedx.json. The expressions
  that occur are all permissive or offer a permissive choice: MIT, Apache-2.0,
  Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, 0BSD, ISC, Zlib,
  Unicode-3.0, BSL-1.0, Unlicense, a few "AND" combinations of those, and
  "MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1-or-later" (the licensee picks MIT or Apache-2.0).

* tesserae_engine.libs/ (libbz2, libfontconfig, libfreetype, libpng15,
  libuuid): shared libraries that the wheel builder (auditwheel) copied in from
  CentOS 7 packages bzip2-libs 1.0.6-13, fontconfig 2.13.0-4.3, freetype
  2.8-14, libpng 1.5.13-8 and libuuid 2.23.2-65 (the wheel's
  dist-info/sboms/auditwheel.cdx.json). That file records the package names and
  versions, not licences, and the wheel carries no copy of these libraries'
  licence texts. The upstream projects publish them under the bzip2 licence
  (bzip2), the fontconfig licence (fontconfig, MIT-style), the FreeType
  License or GPL-2.0 at the user's choice (FreeType), the PNG Reference Library
  License version 1 (libpng 1.5) and BSD-3-Clause (libuuid, from util-linux);
  the texts of the FreeType and libpng licences are also in Pillow's
  dist-info/licenses/LICENSE (section 3).


3. Runtime dependencies (pyproject.toml, `dependencies`, and what they need)

Version ranges are those of pyproject.toml. The licence is the one the
installed release declares in its metadata (License-Expression, License or the
"License ::" classifier) and the one in its dist-info/licenses file, where it
has one.

* tesserae-engine >=0.6.11,<0.7: MIT. https://github.com/mindderivative/tess-re
  (bundled assets: section 2)

* tesserae-el >=0.2.0,<0.3: MIT. https://github.com/mindderivative/tess-el

* tesserae-dl >=0.2.0,<0.3: MIT. https://github.com/mindderivative/tess-dl

* tesserae-utils[image] >=0.2.1,<0.3: MIT.
  https://github.com/mindderivative/tess-utils (the image extra needs pillow,
  which the shell also names itself)

* loguru >=0.7.3,<0.8: MIT. https://github.com/Delgan/loguru (the wheel
  declares MIT in its classifiers and carries no licence file)

* inotify-simple >=2.0.1,<3: BSD-2-Clause.
  https://github.com/chrisjbillington/inotify_simple

* dbus-fast >=2.24,<4: MIT. https://github.com/bluetooth-devices/dbus-fast

* jeepney >=0.9,<0.10: MIT. https://gitlab.com/takluyver/jeepney

* pillow >=11,<14: MIT-CMU, as declared by 13.0.0, the release in uv.lock (the
  licence file of the installed wheel decides for any other release in the
  range). https://python-pillow.org
  The wheel bundles native libraries in pillow.libs/: libXau, libavif,
  libbrotlicommon, libbrotlidec, libfreetype, libharfbuzz, libjpeg, liblcms2,
  liblzma, libopenjp2, libpng16, libsharpyuv, libtiff, libwebp, libwebpdemux,
  libwebpmux, libxcb, libzstd (FreeType, HarfBuzz, Little CMS 2, libjpeg-turbo,
  libpng, libtiff, libwebp, libavif, OpenJPEG, libxcb, libXau, brotli, xz,
  zstd). Their licences are in the wheel's dist-info/licenses/LICENSE and
  dist-info/sboms/pillow-*.cdx.json; the SBOM lists FreeType as FTL, HarfBuzz
  and Little CMS 2 as MIT, libjpeg-turbo as IJG and BSD-3-Clause, libwebp as
  BSD-3-Clause, OpenJPEG and libavif as BSD-2-Clause, libtiff as libtiff, libxcb
  as X11, zlib as Zlib and FriBiDi as LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Development and documentation tools (pytest, ruff, mypy, mkdocs, ...) are not
shipped and not needed at run time.
